<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lombard League</h1><p class="st-meta">1167 CE – 1250 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of northern Italian city-republics that defeated Frederick Barbarossa at Legnano in 1176 and won self-government from the emperors.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1167, according to tradition in an oath sworn at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oath-of-pontida">Pontida</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-cremona">Cremona</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-bergamo">Bergamo</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a> and other cities formed a league against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, absorbing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veronese-league">Veronese League</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii">Pope Alexander III</a> supported it, and the new city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-alessandria">Alessandria</a> was named after him.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league was an alliance of communes with a council of rectors from member cities, a shared war chest and joint armies, rather than a single state. Its forces defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Barbarossa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Legnano</a> in 1176, forcing the Truce of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1177 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-constance">Peace of Constance</a> in 1183, which recognised the cities' rights to elect their own officials.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The league was revived in 1226 against Frederick II, who defeated it at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cortenuova">Cortenuova</a> in 1237 but failed to break the cities. After Frederick's death in 1250 it faded away, as the communes turned to wars among themselves and to rule by lords.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lombard-league.jpg" alt="Lombard League" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Milan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1167 CE – 1250 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Societas Lombardiae</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=lombard-league" aria-label="Lombard League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4959 602 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lombard League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5261 831h0M5218 830h0M5229 694h0M5238 840h0M5242 828h0M5229 823h0M5231 843h0M5246 851h0M5261 831h0M5282 832h0M5290 824h0M5274 828h0M5271 860h0M5226 835h0M5200 834h0M5205 847h0M5205 831h0M5257 840h0M5277 849h0M5261 855h0M5254 854h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5279 858h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5279 858h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=lombard-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
